{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"cbb1643ed05543a3","x":-160,"y":-380,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Campaign Ideas"},
		{"id":"422aa91a238ae6f7","x":-540,"y":-220,"width":350,"height":220,"type":"text","text":"The plague,\nNo memory, post apocalyptic, must figure out what happened based on the items they currently have, memories return randomly?\n\nJason Bourne X The Last of Us"},
		{"id":"48753fb531c38497","x":-190,"y":-225,"width":330,"height":305,"type":"text","text":"Divine Assassins\nOne day gods disappear, divine casters gimped, healing etc sky rocket prices, arcane flourishing, party is granted divine magic. One minor deity has escaped the problem. Promises greater power in exchange.\nwork your way up the pyramid\nis actually a devil trying to take over\n"},
		{"id":"4d278460723366d7","x":140,"y":-225,"width":340,"height":285,"type":"text","text":"Storm of the century\nShipwrecked, not on material plane? Hex crawl, trying to get back to material plane. Scatter their ship pieces, make it a base building game.\nDangerous to be out at night, and if they leave the ship too long it will be scavenged for parts."},
		{"id":"984611af1c63b0ba","x":-220,"y":80,"width":323,"height":380,"type":"text","text":"Keepers of the Strand\nForgotten corner of astral plane, KOS is organization keeping an eye on different timelines (the umbrella academy), the commission. Sometimes the strands get very back out of shape. Fix strands so they can be woven correctly.\nHelldivers? Go in, do the mission, call for extraction.\nMotives are clear cut? Or is there a narrative they are trying to push?\n(mini dungeons, noir, political intrigue)"},
		{"id":"5f88aab603bcc64e","x":-543,"y":44,"width":323,"height":453,"type":"text","text":"City of Last Light\nEndless night, crops dying, attempting to follow day light. Becoming more rapid. The pattern of light loss is a circle. Map tracks progression, that they find in their town.\n\"City of last light\" has the person who is the focus/behind the problem.\nThe ruler made a bargain so they are the only food producer?\nMystery to rulers as well?\nConflict between sun god and god of darkness?\n"},
		{"id":"ca1c2e4372fb7b41","x":142,"y":80,"width":398,"height":500,"type":"text","text":"The Revolution\nModern tech, magic used by common people, terrible housing crisis, other kingdoms drained because everyone has left looking to live out their dreams.\nMonarch behind all this is still in the shadows\nParty working in mines, find a secret that the company wants to keep quiet. Caught between revolutionaries and the corporation/government\n\nSabotage, espionage, thievery, extraction, chases, fetch quests, political intrigue (trying to turn people), uncover moles, escape militia"},
		{"id":"c3e33475746d4d1b","x":-540,"y":497,"width":376,"height":383,"type":"text","text":"Mega dungeon crawl \nplanar black hole, some giant demon under there, causing planes of existance to crash together. \n\nFire hotter, rain more frequent/heavier, things weigh less (fire plane, water and astral), extraplanar creatures invading material plane \nStarting town is within radius of dungeon.\nMust deal with traps, variety of planes thrown into blender... all sorts of monsters, items..\nPlane by level of dungeon, or multiple planes in one\n\nlast battle on highest peak of lowest dungeon\n\n"},
		{"id":"9911a6374300cb40","x":-135,"y":580,"width":476,"height":413,"type":"text","text":"The MTRD\nPlayers are badasses in the library. Magical Text Recovery Department.\nGet books at any cost. \nSometimes books forgotten to return, othertimes actually trying to steal books.\nMTRD crashing through your door is scary. A little of minority report vibes.\nStart with kobolds who stole book about dragons..\nChance of unsolvable case, book checked out prior to libraries existence, and never returned.\n\nThrough plot? Episodic?"},
		{"id":"aa7d9895876f958b","x":360,"y":597,"width":440,"height":583,"type":"text","text":"The Shattering\nMaterial plane destroyed, chasms everywhere, astral abysses.. City in the north is the center point. Closer to the city, the more chasms there are.\n10 years to the day since, players dream of divine being giving them a key to a building in the city. Then they have the key.\nThey meet each other on their way there. \nTravelling is very dangerous, its own adventure.\n\nThe city is now actually 4 different floating islands, 1 government center with strong bridges to barracks island. Operate the same.\n3rd island, dangerous crime family taken over, the trading/industrial district.  bridge highly guarded, goods in and out are very controlled.\n4th island is shrouded in mystery since the shattering. Keys to address on 4th island.\nArcane but more fantasy?\n\nparadise or horrorscape?"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}